# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Two reasons to care:
#   1. Secrets. api-key.txt must never be copied into an image layer -- layers
#      persist in the image history even if a later step deletes the file, so
#      anyone who pulls the image could recover the key. It is supplied at run
#      time instead, as a bind mount or an environment variable.
#   2. Size and cache. Excluding the virtualenv and generated data keeps the
#      build context small and stops unrelated changes from busting the layer
#      cache on every rebuild.

# --- secrets ---
api-key.txt

# --- local virtualenv (platform-specific, must not enter a Linux image) ---
.venv/
venv/

# --- generated data (mounted as volumes at run time) ---
dataset/
results/

# --- python artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- version control and editors ---
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- docs ---
*.md
